WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.722
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A two.

2
00:00:06.022 --> 00:00:09.501
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:16.517
Unit twenty: Past Simple Questions and Negatives. Today you will ask and answer about the past with did and didn't.

4
00:00:16.817 --> 00:00:19.492
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.433 --> 00:00:23.585
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:25.033
Did.

7
00:00:26.017 --> 00:00:28.655
Did means the helping verb for past questions.

8
00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:30.239
Did you go?

9
00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:33.247
Your turn. Say: Did.

10
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:36.718
Did.

11
00:00:37.483 --> 00:00:38.299
Didn't.

12
00:00:39.283 --> 00:00:40.679
Didn't means did not.

13
00:00:41.283 --> 00:00:42.354
I didn't go.

14
00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:45.509
Your turn. Say: Didn't.

15
00:00:48.367 --> 00:00:49.124
Didn't.

16
00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:50.571
Go.

17
00:00:51.583 --> 00:00:53.444
Go means to move to a place.

18
00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:55.399
Did you go to school?

19
00:00:55.983 --> 00:00:58.392
Your turn. Say: Go.

20
00:01:01.233 --> 00:01:01.991
Go.

21
00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:03.368
Went.

22
00:01:04.383 --> 00:01:06.081
Went means the past of go.

23
00:01:06.683 --> 00:01:07.812
I went to the park.

24
00:01:08.417 --> 00:01:10.372
Your turn. Say: Went.

25
00:01:13.233 --> 00:01:14.118
Went.

26
00:01:14.883 --> 00:01:15.954
Yesterday.

27
00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:19.159
Yesterday means the day before today.

28
00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:21.320
Did you study yesterday?

29
00:01:21.917 --> 00:01:24.430
Your turn. Say: Yesterday.

30
00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:28.291
Yesterday.

31
00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:29.923
Question.

32
00:01:30.917 --> 00:01:33.857
Question means a sentence that asks for information.

33
00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:35.881
Ask me a question.

34
00:01:36.483 --> 00:01:38.857
Your turn. Say: Question.

35
00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:42.678
Question.

36
00:01:43.417 --> 00:01:44.464
Negative.

37
00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:47.113
Negative means saying no.

38
00:01:47.717 --> 00:01:49.705
A negative sentence uses didn't.

39
00:01:50.317 --> 00:01:52.772
Your turn. Say: Negative.

40
00:01:55.633 --> 00:01:56.646
Negative.

41
00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:58.280
Answer.

42
00:01:59.283 --> 00:02:01.515
Answer means a reply to a question.

43
00:02:02.117 --> 00:02:03.501
Give a short answer.

44
00:02:04.117 --> 00:02:07.094
Your turn. Say: Answer.

45
00:02:09.933 --> 00:02:10.772
Answer.

46
00:02:11.567 --> 00:02:15.380
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:16.217 --> 00:02:19.833
Visal, what did you do last weekend? What didn't you do?

48
00:02:20.917 --> 00:02:30.491
I went to the market, but I didn't go to the cinema. We use did and didn't with the base verb. The main verb does not take -ed or the past form.

49
00:02:31.583 --> 00:02:33.060
How do we make questions?

50
00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:45.364
Did + subject + base verb: Did you go? What did you eat? Where did she go? The word order is question word, did, subject and base verb.

51
00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:47.718
How do we answer?

52
00:02:48.817 --> 00:03:01.183
With short answers: Yes, I did. No, I didn't. We always use the same helping verb. A common mistake is Did you went. The verb must be go because did already shows the past.

53
00:03:02.333 --> 00:03:03.903
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:09.931
Grammar focus: Past simple questions: Did plus subject plus base verb.

55
00:03:10.231 --> 00:03:11.418
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:12.117 --> 00:03:13.861
Did you go to the market yesterday?

57
00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:16.343
I didn't go to the cinema.

58
00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:18.983
What did she eat for lunch?

59
00:03:19.933 --> 00:03:28.649
Questions: Did + subject + base verb. Negatives: didn't + base verb. After did and didn't the main verb is not in the past form.

60
00:03:29.383 --> 00:03:32.964
Be careful! Don't say: Did you went there?

61
00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:36.911
Say: Did you go there?

62
00:03:37.211 --> 00:03:39.187
Use the base verb after did.

63
00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.838
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:43.633 --> 00:03:44.425
Did You…?.

65
00:03:44.725 --> 00:03:47.738
Did you go to the market yesterday? Yes, I did.

66
00:03:48.733 --> 00:03:51.151
I didn't go to the cinema because I was tired.

67
00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:54.155
What did your sister eat for lunch?

68
00:03:55.167 --> 00:03:58.072
She didn't eat rice, but she ate some noodles.

69
00:03:59.067 --> 00:04:01.893
Did they come by bus? No, they didn't.

70
00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:06.711
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:09.735
blank you go to school yesterday?

72
00:04:10.035 --> 00:04:12.853
A, Do. B, Did. C, Does.

73
00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:18.063
The answer is B: Did.

74
00:04:19.217 --> 00:04:20.984
I blank see him last week.

75
00:04:21.284 --> 00:04:24.241
A, didn't. B, don't. C, wasn't.

76
00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.776
The answer is A: didn't.

77
00:04:30.917 --> 00:04:32.617
Did she go? blank

78
00:04:32.917 --> 00:04:36.733
A, Yes, she did.. B, Yes, she went.. C, Yes, she does..

79
00:04:40.267 --> 00:04:42.638
The answer is A: Yes, she did..

80
00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:45.539
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:45.839 --> 00:04:49.992
A, Did you went?. B, Did you go?. C, Do you went?.

82
00:04:53.533 --> 00:04:55.753
The answer is B: Did you go?.

83
00:04:56.917 --> 00:04:59.752
According to the reading, what did the sister eat?

84
00:05:00.052 --> 00:05:03.183
A, noodles. B, rice. C, soup.

85
00:05:06.733 --> 00:05:08.884
The answer is A: noodles.

86
00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:13.194
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:14.050 --> 00:05:16.772
What did you do last weekend? What didn't you do?

88
00:05:25.583 --> 00:05:27.200
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:38.653
Last weekend I went to the beach and swam in the sea. I didn't go to the market, and I didn't do my homework. I use went for the past of go and didn't + base verb for the negative.

90
00:05:38.953 --> 00:05:40.616
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:41.517 --> 00:05:48.349
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and past simple questions: did plus subject plus base verb.

92
00:05:48.649 --> 00:05:51.951
Today's value is honesty. Always tell the truth.

93
00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:54.950
See you in Unit twenty-one. Goodbye!

94
00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:59.017
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

